          "first": {
            "seq": 8,
            "text": "Act as an expert frontend developer and UX/UI designer. Build a complete, production-ready, classic minimalist personal portfolio website. \n\n### Core Tech Stack\n* HTML5, CSS3 (using modern layouts like Flexbox/Grid), and Vanilla JavaScript.\n* Do not use heavy external frameworks, but you may use a lightweight CDN link for smooth animations (like GSAP or Motion One) if it helps keep the code clean and performant.\n\n### Design System & Layout\n* Aesthetic: Extreme minimalism. Editorial feel, high contrast, generous whitespace, and sharp typography.\n* Color Palette: Pure black, pure white, and one subtle accent tone (e.g., #707070 or #E5E5E5) for borders/muted text. \n* Structure: A single-page scroll or clean multi-section layout containing:\n  1. Hero: Bold typography statement (e.g., \"Name — Creative Developer\") with a subtle entrance animation.\n  2. Selected Work: A grid or list of project items. On hover, show a subtle preview effect or reveal project details.\n  3. About/Experience: A clean two-column layout separating personal statement and timeline/skills.\n  4. Contact: A minimal footer with direct email link and social hooks.\n\n### Interactive Animations (The \"Wow\" Factor)\nImplement smooth, native-feeling animations that enhance—rather than distract from—the minimalism:\n* Custom Cursor: A minimal magnetic or trailing dot cursor that reacts when hovering over clickable links.\n* Reveal on Scroll: Sections or text lines fade and slide up cleanly as they enter the viewport.\n* Hover States: Smooth transitions for links (e.g., underlines that slide in from the left and exit to the right) and project items.\n\n### Technical Requirements\n* Provide the complete code split cleanly into `index.html`, `style.css`, and `app.js`.\n* Ensure perfect responsiveness across mobile, tablet, and desktop screens.\n* Optimize for performance: use CSS hardware acceleration (`transform`, `opacity`) for animations to prevent lag.\n* Include clear code comments explaining how to swap out placeholder text and project images. Don't take more than 5 minutes"
